  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently, the \"allow declarative shadow roots\" opt-in works in the following way:\n- It is set when the document is created - specifically set to false in XHR and old HTML setting methods, and true everywhere else\n- It sticks to the document, surviving clones and `document.open`\n\nI think this is overly complex and we can instead say that `document.open` always supports DSD, which makes it so that we don't need to keep a flag on the document.\n\n This keeps the intent of this flag which is to allow it for normal parsing but prevent it for when applying fragments using one of the legacy methods (`innerHTML`, `XHR` etc)",
